{
  "hostname": "BL-PR-FL2",
  "reason": "Confirm whether floor 2 printer is offline per KB-022"
}

{
  "query": "desktop no network connection wired ethernet",
  "reason": "Find article for desktop network issue"
}

{
  "summary": "Reported: James O'Connor (Warehouse Supervisor, Operations, user_id 8, America/Chicago, hours 06:00-14:00) says his desktop BL-DT-0108 is not on the network and floor 2 printer BL-PR-FL2 is down. Triage P2, user blocked. Checked: account active, not locked, sign-in not blocked, VPN access OK. BL-DT-0108 (Win 11 desktop, wired): online=false, last check-in 2026-10-09T13:07 UTC, no warnings, disk fine. BL-PR-FL2: online=false, last check-in 2026-10-09T10:07 UTC, no warnings/errors reported. Found: two separate devices offline that are likely on the same floor. This may be a floor 2 network segment/switch/drop issue, not two separate device faults. No KB covers wired desktop connectivity loss (KB-014 is Wi-Fi only). I've asked the user to check the desktop's network cable and link light, restart the desktop, have the printer's screen checked for errors, power-cycle the printer for 30 s, and check its cable (KB-022). Still needed: see whether other floor 2 devices/users are offline, check the switch/port for the floor 2 drops, and then fix the desktop and printer connectivity. If more users are affected, consider raising to P1.",
  "reason": "Desktop wired connectivity is not covered by a KB, and two devices are offline at once, which points to a possible floor network fault that needs Tier 2."
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi James, sorry about the rough morning. I checked both: your desktop and the floor 2 printer (BL-PR-FL2) are both showing offline on our end. Since both went down at the same time, there may be a network problem on floor 2, so I've sent this to our Tier 2 team to look into. While you wait, please try these: 1) Make sure the network cable is plugged in firmly at the back of your desktop and at the wall, and check whether the light next to the port is on. Then restart the desktop. 2) For the printer, look at its screen for errors like a paper jam, no paper or toner, or an open door, and clear any you find. Then turn it off for 30 seconds, turn it back on, and check that its network cable is plugged in with the light on. If either one comes back, or you notice other people on floor 2 have lost their connection too, reply here so we can update Tier 2.",
  "internal_note": "User 8, account active and fine. BL-DT-0108 (wired desktop): offline, last check-in 13:07 UTC, no warnings. BL-PR-FL2: offline, last check-in 10:07 UTC, no warnings. Both offline at once suggests a possible floor 2 network/switch problem. No KB covers wired desktop connectivity (KB-014 is Wi-Fi only). Gave the user KB-022 printer steps and basic cable/restart checks. Escalated to Tier 2 (escalation id 1) to check the floor 2 switch/ports and whether other users are affected. Consider P1 if several users are blocked.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-022",
    "KB-014"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
